1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,160
With Sous, AI agents buy from Valio Aimo for a kitchen.

2
00:00:04,328 --> 00:00:06,647
The question is what they may do alone.

3
00:00:07,299 --> 00:00:11,581
There are three answers: order alone, ask a person, or refuse.

4
00:00:11,660 --> 00:00:13,325
Here's each one, live.

5
00:00:13,799 --> 00:00:16,224
Alone first, with the brief's own example:

6
00:00:16,224 --> 00:00:19,112
a thousand litres of lactose-free milk for Monday.

7
00:00:19,192 --> 00:00:22,140
Sous checks live price and stock, signs a fixed price,

8
00:00:22,140 --> 00:00:23,832
and the agent orders by itself.

9
00:00:26,099 --> 00:00:29,540
Now a harder one: whipping cream for Monday's panna cotta.

10
00:00:29,663 --> 00:00:34,632
The search covers over seventeen thousand products without calling Valio's systems,

11
00:00:34,632 --> 00:00:38,044
and the quote shows the usual cream's cut-off has passed.

12
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:40,349
So the agent asks for substitutes,

13
00:00:40,349 --> 00:00:42,459
and says the cream is for a recipe.

14
00:00:42,605 --> 00:00:46,574
The pick comes back as a signed quote: a fixed price,

15
00:00:46,574 --> 00:00:49,047
with reliability, origin and CO₂.

16
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:51,510
The agent orders, and the order waits,

17
00:00:51,510 --> 00:00:53,780
because what it's for decides the swap.

18
00:00:53,887 --> 00:00:58,544
Coffee could take any cream of the same kind; a recipe needs the chef.

19
00:00:58,625 --> 00:01:02,068
Anything off the usual waits too: bigger quantities,

20
00:01:02,068 --> 00:01:05,378
later delivery, a price jump, different allergens.

21
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,027
Valio Aimo sees the order, but doesn't decide it.

22
00:01:09,152 --> 00:01:13,650
The chef gets the reason in plain words, in Finnish too,

23
00:01:13,650 --> 00:01:15,739
and approves on the phone.

24
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:19,380
And some things are never allowed.

25
00:01:19,607 --> 00:01:23,096
A school's order over its limit is refused outright,

26
00:01:23,096 --> 00:01:25,981
and so is an agent approving its own order.

27
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:29,529
All of it comes from the mandate the buyer issued,

28
00:01:29,529 --> 00:01:31,339
run by plain code in four tiers.

29
00:01:31,468 --> 00:01:34,580
No language model approves an order or relaxes a rule.

30
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:37,739
On our own test cases, not a held-out set:

31
00:01:37,739 --> 00:01:40,440
zero mandate violations across five models.

32
00:01:40,452 --> 00:01:45,563
And it's open: MCP, OpenAPI, Peppol, MIT.

33
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:52,020
Next: buyer login, Valio Aimo's order API and contract prices.

34
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:52,920
Sous.

35
00:01:53,011 --> 00:01:56,469
Agents do the buying, and the customer stays in control.
